{"analysis":"Version 6 (71.9) scored below version 5 (72.8). Calling plain plans neutral moved some neutral texts out of positive, but it cost more positive recall (167 to 155). Plans stay as in version 5.

Version 7 is version 5 with one targeted change on the negative side. About 37 to 42 negative texts are still predicted neutral, and many of them are news of trouble: manslaughter charge, under investigation, 'Problems for Newcastle', close to war, punished in scandal. Version 4, which had a charge-news negative example, reached the highest negative recall (148). That version's positive losses came from its 'dry listings' line, not from the negative example.

So I'll swap the obvious Sharknado example for the Caitlyn Jenner charge example. I'll also add charge, scandal, investigation and problems to the negative rule and cues. Positive and neutral wording stays exactly as in version 5.","question":"What overall feeling does the tweet's author show toward its topic: positive, neutral, or negative?","rule":"Positive includes mild warmth: looking forward to a plan, friendly invitations ('see you there!'), good-luck wishes, excited fan outbursts, holiday fun, tributes to the dead, and news of wins, releases, tours or new products. Neutral is dry information, logistics, commercial ads, plain ticket sales, questions, speculation and calm analysis. Negative needs explicit annoyance, insults, disappointment, worry, personal setbacks, or news of harm or trouble: deaths, attacks, losses, charges, scandals, investigations, protests. Hypothetical sadness, self-mocking stress and ironic exaggeration stay neutral.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Any warmth, anticipation, praise, well-wishing or tribute, or good news such as wins, records, releases and launches.","examples":["It’s Tuesday night in Athens! AKA karaoke night at the Volstead so come see me!!","Guess who's going to see Foo Fighters on Tuesday!!!!! (ME)","New iPhones, iPad Pro, and Apple TV on the way today at 10 A.M. (PDT)! #AppleEvent","Happy Birthday Wilt Chamberlain may you rest in peace"],"cues":"see you, come see, good luck, can't wait, love, best, awesome, happy, tribute, new album, wins, flailing, OMG, :)","not_for":"Dry schedules, ads or ticket listings with no warmth (neutral); 'can't wait' used sarcastically (negative)."},"neutral":{"what":"Factual updates, logistics, ads, questions, predictions, and opinions without emotional words.","examples":["Special Labor Day COOL OUT goes down TOMORROW NIGHT @ the Gin Mill 10-2","Pochettino should have started Alli. He'll probably do a Kane and keep him on the bench till November. Might be too late for him this term","when I go to the Foo Fighters concert in October in Atlanta I'm gonna be so sad if don't get to meet Dave Grohl somehow"],"cues":"tomorrow night, tickets, specials, ?, should have, may, probably, if","not_for":"Invitations or plans with clear enthusiasm (positive); explicit complaints, insults, or reports of harm or trouble (negative)."},"negative":{"what":"Anger, sadness, worry, insults, personal disappointment or inconvenience, and news of deaths, attacks, losses, charges, scandals or protests.","examples":["Caitlyn Jenner May Face Manslaughter Charge in Malibu Crash I read it on @user #video: ","@user so the thing next Thursday isn't free, you'd have to pay $15 to get in since you don't go to UMBC :/ and it ends at 11:30""],"cues":"sucks, wtf, hate, pity, nervous, argh, ugh, #fml, crying, :/, :(, killed, charge, problems, investigation, delayed, boo, protest","not_for":"Calm arguments, hedged speculation, playful exaggeration, or RIP tributes (neutral or positive)."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 8 (73.2) scored slightly below version 7 (73.6). Anchoring neutral with a harsh sports critique cut neutral-to-negative errors (29 to 22), but more true negatives slipped to neutral (30 to 39). Negative recall fell from 150 to 141.

Annotators often do treat critical commentary as negative, so version 9 returns to version 7's structure: the milder Pochettino neutral anchor, and the trouble-news negative example.

The only change is to the negative cues: sarcastic pity ('feel sorry for'), 'meltdown' and 'not happy'. These appeared in missed negatives and are unlikely to pull neutral texts over. Positive and neutral wording stay as in version 7, which gave the best balance.","question":"What overall feeling does the tweet's author show toward its topic: positive, neutral, or negative?","rule":"Positive includes mild warmth: looking forward to a plan, friendly invitations ('see you there!'), good-luck wishes, excited fan outbursts, holiday fun, tributes to the dead, and news of wins, releases, tours or new products. Neutral is dry information, logistics, commercial ads, plain ticket sales, questions, speculation and calm analysis. Negative needs explicit annoyance, insults, disappointment, worry, personal setbacks, or news of harm or trouble: deaths, attacks, losses, charges, scandals, investigations, protests. Hypothetical sadness, self-mocking stress and ironic exaggeration stay neutral.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Any warmth, anticipation, praise, well-wishing or tribute, or good news such as wins, records, releases and launches.","examples":["It’s Tuesday night in Athens! AKA karaoke night at the Volstead so come see me!!","Guess who's going to see Foo Fighters on Tuesday!!!!! (ME)","New iPhones, iPad Pro, and Apple TV on the way today at 10 A.M. (PDT)! #AppleEvent","Happy Birthday Wilt Chamberlain may you rest in peace"],"cues":"see you, come see, good luck, can't wait, love, best, awesome, happy, tribute, new album, wins, flailing, OMG, :)","not_for":"Dry schedules, ads or ticket listings with no warmth (neutral); 'can't wait' used sarcastically (negative)."},"neutral":{"what":"Factual updates, logistics, ads, questions, predictions, and opinions without emotional words.","examples":["Special Labor Day COOL OUT goes down TOMORROW NIGHT @ the Gin Mill 10-2","Pochettino should have started Alli. He'll probably do a Kane and keep him on the bench till November. Might be too late for him this term","when I go to the Foo Fighters concert in October in Atlanta I'm gonna be so sad if don't get to meet Dave Grohl somehow"],"cues":"tomorrow night, tickets, specials, ?, should have, may, probably, if","not_for":"Invitations or plans with clear enthusiasm (positive); explicit complaints, insults, or reports of harm or trouble (negative)."},"negative":{"what":"Anger, sadness, worry, insults, personal disappointment or inconvenience, and news of deaths, attacks, losses, charges, scandals or protests.","examples":["Caitlyn Jenner May Face Manslaughter Charge in Malibu Crash I read it on @user #video: ","@user so the thing next Thursday isn't free, you'd have to pay $15 to get in since you don't go to UMBC :/ and it ends at 11:30""],"cues":"sucks, wtf, hate, pity, feel sorry for, not happy, meltdown, nervous, argh, ugh, #fml, crying, :/, :(, killed, charge, problems, investigation, delayed, boo, protest","not_for":"Calm arguments, hedged speculation, playful exaggeration, or RIP tributes (neutral or positive)."}}}
